WEBVTT

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:33.001
and the dream of finding that passion
and, "Go and flourish,"

00:10:33.025 --> 00:10:34.838
and that's part of what happened?

00:10:34.862 --> 00:10:37.923
DB: Well, first, there was
a sort of left-wing individualization,

00:10:37.947 --> 00:10:39.685
which was more social and lifestyle.

00:10:39.709 --> 00:10:43.243
There was also a right-wing version,
which was about economic deregulation.

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:45.118
And I do think the Baby Boomers, say,

00:10:45.142 --> 00:10:48.015
were living off some of
the social capital they grew up with,

00:10:48.039 --> 00:10:49.642
the communities and institutions.

00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:51.441
But then, when we came time, frankly,

00:10:51.465 --> 00:10:53.625
for my generation
to pass it down to our kids,

00:10:53.649 --> 00:10:54.997
we gave them nothing.

00:10:55.021 --> 00:10:57.668
I spent a lot of time looking
at commencement addresses,

00:10:57.692 --> 00:11:00.363
because that's how our culture
passes down moral lessons: